# Environment
#
# The glob matters as much as the base name.  ``.env`` alone left the
# production VPS carrying seven UNTRACKED-but-not-ignored copies of it
# (.env.bak, .env.bak.<epoch> x5, .env.save) — every one a verbatim snapshot of
# the live secrets: Binance keys, KMS config, Firebase credentials, the ops
# bearer token.  Untracked is not safe; it means a single ``git add -A`` run on
# the box stages production secrets into a commit.  Ignore every derivative,
# not just the canonical name.  ``.env.example`` stays tracked as the template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

